menu "Wi-Fi bridge"

    config WIFI_BRIDGE_SETUP_AP_SSID
        string "Setup network name"
        default "Netlab-Fraga"
        help
            Name of the Wi-Fi network the device opens when it needs to be configured
            (1 to 32 characters). Two devices with the same name in range are hard to
            tell apart: change it on the second one.

    config WIFI_BRIDGE_SETUP_AP_PASSWORD
        string "Setup network password"
        default "netlabsetup"
        help
            WPA2 password of the setup network (8 to 63 characters), or empty for an open
            network. It protects the moment you type your router's password, so change it
            if you do not want neighbors who read this repository to be able to join.

    config WIFI_BRIDGE_SETUP_AP_MAX_CLIENTS
        int "Maximum devices on the setup network"
        range 1 4
        default 2

    config WIFI_BRIDGE_FALLBACK_SECONDS
        int "Open the setup network after this many seconds without a connection"
        range 20 3600
        default 90
        help
            When a saved network cannot be reached (the device moved to another house, or
            the router is down), the setup network opens after this delay so a new router
            can be chosen. It closes again on its own once the device is back online.
            If the saved network is not found at all (not in range), it is forgotten and the
            device restarts straight into setup mode instead.

endmenu
